#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:2
msgid "Contributing Guide"
msgstr "贡献指南"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:4
msgid ""
"Thank you for your interest in contributing to LMCache! We welcome and "
"accept all kinds of contributions, no matter how small or large. There "
"are several ways you can contribute to the project:"
msgstr "感谢您对为 LMCache 做出贡献的兴趣！我们欢迎并接受各种类型的贡献，无论大小。您可以通过以下几种方式为项目做出贡献："

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:6
msgid "Identify and report any issues or bugs"
msgstr "识别并报告任何问题或错误"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:7
msgid "Request or add support for a new model"
msgstr "请求或添加对新模型的支持"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:8
msgid "Suggest or implement new features"
msgstr "建议或实现新功能"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:9
msgid "Improve documentation or contribute a how-to guide"
msgstr "改进文档或贡献操作指南"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:11
msgid ""
"A comprehensive list of good first issues can be found in the issue "
"`[Onboarding]: Welcoming contributors with good first issues! "
"<https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/issues/627>`_."
msgstr "可以在议题 `[入职]: 欢迎贡献者，提供适合首次贡献的问题！<https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/issues/627>`_ 中找到适合首次贡献的问题的完整列表。"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:13
msgid ""
"If you'd like to support our community further, then answering queries, "
"offering PR reviews, and assisting others are also impactful ways to "
"contribute and take LMCache further."
msgstr "如果您想进一步支持我们的社区，回答问题、提供 PR 审查和帮助他人也是有影响力的贡献方式，可以推动 LMCache 发展。"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:15
msgid ""
"Finally, you can support us by raising awareness about LMCache. Feel free"
" to share our blog posts, check out our handle on X at `LMCache "
"<https://x.com/lmcache>`_ and see the latest of what we are up to. If "
"using LMCache helped your project or product in any way, you can simply "
"offer your appreciation by starring our repository!"
msgstr "最后，您可以通过提高对 LMCache 的认识来支持我们。欢迎分享我们的博客文章，在 X 上关注我们的账号 `LMCache <https://x.com/lmcache>`_，了解我们的最新动态。如果使用 LMCache 对您的项目或产品有任何帮助，您可以通过给我们的仓库加星来表达您的赞赏！"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:18
msgid "License"
msgstr "许可证"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:20
msgid ""
"See the `LICENSE <https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/blob/dev/LICENSE>`_ "
"file for details."
msgstr "详细信息请参阅 `LICENSE <https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/blob/dev/LICENSE>`_ 文件。"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:23
msgid "Code of Conduct"
msgstr "行为准则"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:25
msgid ""
"This project adheres to the `Code of Conduct "
"<https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/blob/dev/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md>`_. By "
"participating, you are expected to uphold this code."
msgstr "本项目遵循 `行为准则 <https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/blob/dev/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md>`_。参与时，您需要遵守此准则。"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:28
msgid "Contribution Guidelines"
msgstr "贡献指南"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:30
msgid ""
"Help on open source projects is always welcome and there is always "
"something that can be improved. For example, documentation (like the text"
" you are reading now) can always use improvement, code can always be "
"clarified, variables or functions can always be renamed or commented on, "
"and there is always a need for more test coverage. If you see something "
"that you think should be fixed, take ownership! Here is how you get "
"started."
msgstr "开源项目总是欢迎帮助，总有可以改进的地方。例如，文档（就像您现在阅读的文本）总是可以改进，代码总是可以更清晰，变量或函数总是可以重命名或添加注释，而且总是需要更多的测试覆盖。如果您看到您认为应该修复的东西，请承担责任！以下是您入门的方法。"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:33
msgid "How Can I Contribute?"
msgstr "如何贡献？"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:35
msgid ""
"When contributing, it's useful to start by looking at `issues "
"<https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/issues>`_. After picking up an issue,"
" writing code, or updating a document, make a pull request and your work "
"will be reviewed and merged. If you're adding a new feature or find a "
"bug, it's best to `write an issue "
"<https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/issues/new>`_ first to discuss it "
"with maintainers."
msgstr "贡献时，从查看 `问题 <https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/issues>`_ 开始很有用。在选择问题、编写代码或更新文档后，创建拉取请求，您的工作将被审查和合并。如果您要添加新功能或发现错误，最好先 `创建问题 <https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/issues/new>`_ 与维护者讨论。"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:37
msgid ""
"If you discover a security vulnerability, please follow the instructions "
"in the `Security doc "
"<https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/blob/dev/SECURITY.md>`_."
msgstr "如果您发现安全漏洞，请遵循 `安全文档 <https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/blob/dev/SECURITY.md>`_ 中的说明。"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:39
msgid ""
"To contribute to this repo, you'll use the Fork and Pull model common in "
"many open source repositories. For details on this process, check out "
"`The GitHub Workflow Guide "
"<https://github.com/kubernetes/community/blob/master/contributors/guide"
"/github-workflow.md>`_ from Kubernetes. In short:"
msgstr "要为此仓库做贡献，您将使用许多开源仓库中常见的 Fork 和 Pull 模型。有关此过程的详细信息，请查看 Kubernetes 的 `GitHub 工作流指南 <https://github.com/kubernetes/community/blob/master/contributors/guide/github-workflow.md>`_。简而言之："

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:41
msgid "Fork the repository"
msgstr "Fork 仓库"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:42
msgid "Create a branch"
msgstr "创建分支"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:43
msgid "Run code style checks and fix any issues"
msgstr "运行代码风格检查并修复任何问题"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:44
msgid "Run unit tests and fix any broken tests"
msgstr "运行单元测试并修复任何失败的测试"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:45
msgid "Submit a pull request with detailed descriptions"
msgstr "提交带有详细描述的拉取请求"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:47
msgid ""
"When your contribution is ready, you can create a pull request. Pull "
"requests are often referred to as \"PRs\". In general, we follow the "
"standard `GitHub pull request <https://help.github.com/en/articles/about-"
"pull-requests>`_ process. Follow the template to provide details about "
"your pull request to the maintainers. It's best to break your "
"contribution into smaller PRs with incremental changes, and include a "
"good description of the changes. We require new unit tests to be "
"contributed with any new functionality added."
msgstr "当您的贡献准备好时，您可以创建拉取请求。拉取请求通常称为 \"PR\"。一般来说，我们遵循标准的 `GitHub 拉取请求 <https://help.github.com/en/articles/about-pull-requests>`_ 流程。遵循模板向维护者提供有关拉取请求的详细信息。最好将您的贡献分解为带有增量更改的较小 PR，并包含对更改的良好描述。我们要求为添加的任何新功能贡献新的单元测试。"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:49
msgid ""
"Before sending pull requests, make sure your changes pass code quality "
"checks and unit tests. These checks will run with the pull request "
"builds. Alternatively, you can run the checks manually on your local "
"machine `as specified in Development <#development>`_ ."
msgstr "在发送拉取请求之前，请确保您的更改通过代码质量检查和单元测试。这些检查将在拉取请求构建时运行。或者，您可以在本地机器上手动运行检查，`如开发部分所述 <#development>`_。"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:52
msgid "DCO and Signed-off-by"
msgstr "DCO 和 Signed-off-by"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:54
msgid ""
"When contributing changes to the project, you must agree to the `DCO "
"<https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/blob/dev/DCO>`_. Commits must include"
" a :code:`Signed-off-by` header which certifies agreement with the terms "
"of the `DCO <https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/blob/dev/DCO>`_."
msgstr "为项目贡献更改时，您必须同意 `DCO <https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/blob/dev/DCO>`_。提交必须包含 :code:`Signed-off-by` 标头，以证明同意 `DCO <https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache/blob/dev/DCO>`_ 的条款。"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:58
msgid ""
"Using :code:`-s` or :code:`--signoff` flag with :code:`git commit` will "
"automatically add this header. The flags can also be used with "
":code:`--amend` if you forget to sign your last commit."
msgstr "在 :code:`git commit` 中使用 :code:`-s` 或 :code:`--signoff` 标志将自动添加此标头。如果您忘记签署上次提交，这些标志也可以与 :code:`--amend` 一起使用。"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:61
msgid "Code Review"
msgstr "代码审查"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:63
msgid ""
"Once you've created a pull request, maintainers will review your code and"
" may make suggestions to fix before merging. It will be easier for your "
"pull request to receive reviews if you consider the criteria the "
"reviewers follow while working. Remember to:"
msgstr "一旦您创建了拉取请求，维护者将审查您的代码，并可能在合并前提出修改建议。如果您在工作时考虑审查者遵循的标准，您的拉取请求将更容易获得审查。请记住："

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:65
msgid "Document the code well to help future contributors and maintainers"
msgstr "编写良好的代码文档以帮助未来的贡献者和维护者"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:66
msgid "Follow the project coding conventions for consistency and best practices"
msgstr "遵循项目编码规范以保持一致性和最佳实践"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:67
msgid "Include sufficient tests to maintain robustness of the code"
msgstr "包含足够的测试以保持代码的健壮性"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:68
msgid ""
"Add or update documentation in :code:`/docs` if PR modifies user facing "
"behavior to help people using LMCache"
msgstr "如果 PR 修改了面向用户的行为，请在 :code:`/docs` 中添加或更新文档，以帮助使用 LMCache 的用户"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:69
msgid "Run coding style checks to ensure consistency and correctness"
msgstr "运行代码风格检查以确保一致性和正确性"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:70
msgid ""
"Run tests locally and ensure they pass and don't break the existing code "
"base"
msgstr "在本地运行测试并确保它们通过且不会破坏现有代码库"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:71
msgid "Write detailed commit messages to help future contributors and maintainers"
msgstr "编写详细的提交消息以帮助未来的贡献者和维护者"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:72
msgid ""
"Break large changes into a logical series of smaller patches, which are "
"easy to understand individually and combine to solve a broader issue"
msgstr "将大型更改拆分为逻辑上的一系列较小补丁，这些补丁易于单独理解并组合起来解决更广泛的问题"

#: ../../source/developer_guide/contributing.rst:76
msgid ""
"Maintainers will perform \"squash and merge\" actions on PRs in this "
"repo, so it doesn't matter how many commits your PR has, as they will end"
" up being a single commit after merging."
msgstr "维护者将对此仓库中的 PR 执行 \"压缩并合并\" 操作，因此您的 PR 有多少次提交并不重要，因为它们在合并后最终会成为单个提交。"

